# Line endings: normalise to LF in the repo regardless of what the working
# copy uses. Without this, committing from Windows can land CRLF in the repo
# and produce whole-file diffs for anyone on another OS.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets — never diffed, never line-ending-converted.
*.png binary
*.webp binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.ico binary
*.woff2 binary

# SVG is text and worth diffing (the favicon is hand-edited).
*.svg text

# NOTE: this repo deliberately does NOT use Git LFS.
#
# The scaffold this project started from shipped a generic .gitattributes that
# routed *.png and *.webp through LFS. That would have broken the production
# site: Vercel does not fetch LFS objects during a build, so it checks out the
# text pointer files and serves those as images — every project screenshot and
# the link-preview image would 404 or render as garbage.
#
# LFS also buys nothing here. The entire binary payload is ~480KB, and images
# are downscaled to WebP by scripts/optimize-images.mjs before they land.
# Do not reintroduce LFS filters without also configuring the host to fetch
# them.
